{
  "schema": "power.model.v1",
  "description": "Research Ravigneaux train with sampled AT range feedback, bounded pressure PI and actual piston/pressure/lock sensing. The controller owns fill/drain valves, vents before conflicting ranges and reports direction, supply, release, apply and confirmed-lock faults. Optional converter lockup uses declared speed hysteresis and pressure feedback. Research Ravigneaux train with resolved planet spin/orbit and a shared shaft-driven hydraulic supply. Each range clutch/brake, plus converter lockup when present, has a compliant oil chamber, moving piston, return spring/damping, elastic stroke stops and contact-derived friction capacity. Explicit fill/drain valves, pump leakage/drag and relief track pressure energy, swept volume, hydraulic work and heat. Prescribed valve schedules are not complete AT control. Tank gauge pressure is zero; parameters, maps and OEM applicability remain unverified. Planet geometry: three synchronous pairs; ring pitch radius 0.1 m; per inner/outer mass 0.3/1 kg and spin inertia 0.000015/0.0005 kg m2; carrier structure 0.03 kg m2 plus orbital inertia 0.0184375 kg m2. Piston front/back areas 0.001/0 m2, nominal stroke 0..0.006 m and contact at 0.002 m are declared research inputs.",
